@startuml HermesDesktopOverSSH
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: offer a desktop GUI agent — Hermes Desktop on the host, its backend inside sbx
' covers: defs/hermes/**
' covers: internal/hermesdesktop/gateway.go
' covers: internal/hermesdesktop/gateway_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/**
' covers: internal/run/**
'
' ── DECISION (2026-10-24, user: "Desktop → sbx over SSH") ───────────────────
' Research (sources in the session report): no desktop agent proveo could offer
' is VM-isolated by default except Cowork, which boots its own VM (Apple
' Virtualization.framework) and moves to cloud execution on 2026-10-06 — wrapping
' it in sbx is the oxymoron the operator named. Codex app = Seatbelt; Goose
' Desktop = optional sandbox-exec; Ollama's app = chat + models, no agent tools.
' Hermes Desktop's own local backend runs tools ON THE HOST unless
' terminal.backend is docker/ssh/modal/daytona, and its plugins are "not
' sandboxed". Hermes Desktop is a client: it can attach to a remote backend
' (Remote gateway URL, SSH, Hermes Cloud). So proveo keeps the backend in sbx
' and the GUI on the host.
'
' ── PROBE H1 (MEASURED 2026-10-24, sbx 0.49.2, proveo/hermes:local) ─────────
'   * The image ships Hermes Agent v0.21.5 with `hermes serve` (JSON-RPC/
'     WebSocket backend for the desktop; --port 9119, --host 127.0.0.1 default;
'     a non-loopback bind always requires password/OAuth since June 2026).
'   * `sbx setup ssh` writes the *.sbx ssh_config (already Included from
'     ~/.ssh/config on this host). `ssh <name>.sbx` lands as root;
'     `ssh hermes@<name>.sbx` (or agent@) lands as uid 1000. Both sessions carry
'     the image ENV (PATH with /opt/hermes/bin, HERMES_HOME=/opt/data).
'   * `ssh -L 19119:127.0.0.1:9119 hermes@<name>.sbx -- hermes serve --skip-build`
'     printed HERMES_BACKEND_READY port=9119; host
'     `curl 127.0.0.1:19119/api/status` → version 0.21.5, auth_required false
'     (loopback bind; only the tunnel reaches it).
'   * A bare probe workload has no seed, so /opt/data was root-owned and had to
'     be chowned to 1000; proveo's real hermes workload seeds it.
'   * sbx itself ships desktop SSH profiles for Codex and Claude Desktop
'     (`sbx setup ssh --auto-create`): desktop-app-over-SSH is an upstream pattern.
'
' ── OPEN (needs the app; not installed on this host) ─────────────────────────
'   H2 Hermes Desktop's SSH gateway type accepts host `hermes@<name>.sbx`, uses
'      the system OpenSSH (so the Included *.sbx config resolves), and starts
'      `hermes serve --ssh-session-token-file … --ssh-owner-nonce …` in the
'      sandbox itself. [Unverified]
'   H3 Whether the app's gateway list can be written by proveo (a file in its
'      user-data dir) or must be added by hand in Settings → Gateways. [Unverified]
'   H4 What the session needs from the running workload: models reach providers
'      through sbx's credential proxy and Ollama through open+forward, exactly
'      as the TUI run does. [Inference]
'
' ── INSTALL (user: "proveo should be able to install it, for macOS and linux:
' fedora/ubuntu/debian") ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED 2026-10-24:
'   * GitHub releases of NousResearch/hermes-agent carry NO assets (v0.22.0–
'     v0.22.5); v0.22.5's tag is unsigned (verified=false) → commit
'     bf0203a794a07aac3ff764972ab9087baa4e4f4e is the integrity anchor.
'   * hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/desktop offers Hermes-Setup.dmg (6.7 MB,
'     sha256 b61e047e…, notarized Developer ID "Brooklyn Nicholson
'     (T2F6S8MF7C)") and a Windows .exe; Linux installs "through the terminal".
'     No published checksums.
'   * The DMG is a bootstrapper, not the app: Hermes.app
'     (com.nousresearch.hermes.setup 0.0.1) downloads scripts/install.sh from
'     raw.githubusercontent.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/<pin> and runs it.
'   * install.sh: --commit SHA pins the clone; --include-desktop builds the
'     Electron app from source (electron-builder: dmg/zip, AppImage/deb/rpm)
'     into <install dir>/apps/desktop/release; uv is sha256-pinned; node and
'     build tools arrive through `hermes pm`. install.sh at bf0203a7 has
'     sha256 99cb3691d55019c6973a7acb775a915648666cc24e483ca827a1cdbb3531a674.
'   * LINUX PROBES (MEASURED, throwaway containers, arm64, install.sh at
'     bf0203a7 run as a non-root user with --commit bf0203a7 --include-desktop
'     --non-interactive --skip-browser --skip-computer-use):
'       ubuntu:24.04 PASS with curl git ca-certificates xz-utils libatomic1
'                    build-essential python3
'       fedora:42    PASS with curl git ca-certificates xz libatomic make
'                    gcc-c++ python3
'       debian:13    PASS with the ubuntu set
'     internal/hermesdesktop pins Tag/Commit/InstallScriptSHA256, maps hosts to
'     these sets (apt: ubuntu, debian, ID_LIKE ubuntu|debian; dnf: fedora) and
'     refuses others; Install runs nothing when install.sh misses the digest.
'     Each failed first on libatomic.so.1 (Hermes' pinned node 26.12.1; its
'     own error names `apt-get install -y libatomic1` / `dnf install -y
'     libatomic`), then on `make` (node-pty's node-gyp rebuild). Output:
'     ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/apps/desktop/release/linux-arm64-unpacked (no
'     AppImage); the launcher entry ($XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/hermes.desktop)
'     appears on the first `hermes desktop`. A fresh install takes minutes.
'   → proveo follows upstream's own path on every OS, pinned harder: fetch
'     install.sh at the pinned commit, check its sha256, run it with --commit
'     <pin> --include-desktop --non-interactive (--skip-browser
'     --skip-computer-use: the host runtime is only the GUI's shell).
'   CAVEAT: this installs a Hermes runtime on the host too, and the app keeps
'   an undeletable "Local" gateway whose tools run on the host. proveo must
'   steer the operator to the sbx gateway (H5, open).
'
' ── BUILT (2026-10-24, user: "devices row: desktop") ────────────────────────
'   * manifest hostDevices accepts `desktop`; defs/hermes declares it, so only
'     hermes's devices row offers it (TestOnlyHermesOffersTheDesktopDevice).
'   * run: picking desktop calls Deps.EnsureDesktop (cmd/proveo/desktop.go):
'     installed → launch argv; missing → the pinned plan is shown and
'     provisionConfirm asks (PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION applies); declined → the
'     run stops with how to proceed and nothing is written.
'   * backend: Input.Desktop swaps the TUI attach for holdForDesktop: `sbx
'     setup ssh`, print `hermes@<name>.sbx`, open the app detached, wait for
'     the stop; Ctrl+C is backend.Stopped, so teardown is the normal one.
'   * --print shows `# desktop` with the setup and the gateway instead of `#
'     agent`.
'   STILL OPEN: H2–H5 need the app on a host (the first `proveo run hermes`
'   with desktop installs it on this Mac after a yes).
'
' ── DESKTOP DEFAULTED TO THE HOST (MEASURED 2026-10-30) ─────────────────────
' A `proveo run hermes` desktop session answered from Nous's free model, and
' Hermes installed llama.cpp + a Qwen 3.8 27B GGUF instead of using the host's
' Ollama. Cause, read from hermes-agent bf0203a7:
'   * The app boots its connections.json PRIMARY; with no registry that is the
'     injected `local` entry = a backend ON THE HOST (~/.hermes, host tools).
'     proveo only printed the gateway, so every chat until the operator picked
'     it ran on the host.
'   * hermes_cli/auth.py resolve_provider: config.yaml model.provider is rung 2;
'     the Nous free tier (`nous/welcome`) is rung 7 and exists only on the local
'     Desktop backend (anon_auth.free_inference_active needs a claim only a
'     native-ticket client makes; an SSH backend never holds one).
'   * hermes_cli/local_runtime: Hermes' own managed llama.cpp runtime. detect.py
'     fingerprints llama-server by /props and skips Ollama by design; models go
'     to <hermes root>/models (host ~/.hermes, or ~/.proveo/hermes/data via the
'     mount when the sbx backend ran it).
'
' ── GATEWAY (2026-10-30, user: "Register + verify", "Proveo-owned userData") ─
' Answers H3. proveo writes <proveo home>/desktop/hermes/connections.json
' (v2: version, primary, lastUsed, launchMode "primary", connections[] with
' {id "proveo-sandbox", kind ssh, label, host <name>.sbx, user hermes}) and
' launches with HERMES_DESKTOP_USER_DATA_DIR pointing there (main.ts reads it
' before userData; upstream install e2e uses it). Consequences:
'   * the operator's own Desktop userData is never written;
'   * Electron's single-instance lock lives in userData ⇒ a second instance;
'   * appearance/OAuth start blank in proveo's window.
' registryPrimaryIsRemote() ⇒ the window dials the SSH primary. [Inference]
' until a desktop run confirms it (H2 still open).
' VERIFY: every 3 s proveo runs `sbx exec -w / <name> -- bash -c <probe>`; the
' probe matches Desktop's `serve --isolated --host 127.0.0.1` (remote-lifecycle.ts
' spawn command) in /proc/*/cmdline ([s]erve keeps the probe from matching
' itself). Attached ⇒ ✓ line. None after 90 s ⇒ one ⚠ naming the host backend.
'
' ── NOUS GUEST (2026-10-30, user: "Sandbox config only") ────────────────────
' entrypoint.sh: `hermes config set nous.guest false` on every hermes start.
' config.py _coerce_config_set_value turns "false" into a YAML bool, which
' anon_auth.guest_allowed reads. The host's ~/.hermes is untouched.
' [Unverified] the image's hermes (v2026.9.24) coerces the same way.

' ── DESIGN (after H2–H4) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   `proveo run hermes` with a `desktop` interface: create the workload as
'   today (seed, credentials, allowlist), skip attaching the TUI, run
'   `sbx setup ssh`, register or print the SSH gateway `hermes@<name>.sbx`,
'   open Hermes Desktop, and hold until Ctrl+C; teardown is the normal one
'   (clone carried home, state saved, sandbox kept or removed by the usual rule).
'   Keys never enter ~/.hermes/.env on the host.
title Hermes Desktop on the host, Hermes backend in sbx — over sbx's own SSH

node "host (macOS)" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "Hermes Desktop\n(GUI client)" as APP <<app>>
  component "ssh hermes@<name>.sbx\n(*.sbx from `sbx setup ssh`)" as SSH <<app>>
}
node "sbx sandbox proveo-hermes-<id>" as SBX <<host>> {
  component "hermes serve\n127.0.0.1:9119" as SERVE <<app>>
  component "tools · files · terminal\n(inside the VM)" as TOOLS <<app>>
}
cloud "providers via sbx credential proxy\nOllama via open+forward" as MODELS <<cloud>>
APP --> SSH : SSH gateway
SSH --> SERVE : tunnel (loopback only)
SERVE --> TOOLS
SERVE --> MODELS
@enduml
